Description: Density and Distribution Function variable-knot Spline estimation,
  DDFS, is a non-parametric method for the simultaneous estimation of both the
  probability density function (pdf) and cumulative distribution function (cdf)
  of a random variable. Leveraging B-spine properties, this method defines a model
  structure under which, both the pdf and cdf spline models share the same set of
  knots and their coefficients are connected. Estimation is then performed through
  an iterative approach that combines constrained maximum likelihood estimation of
  the coefficients with sequential minimum bias driven estimation of the knots. A
  comprehensive account of the method, including its asymptotic properties and an
  extensive numerical study, can be found in Dimitrova et al. (2025) (forthcoming).
